{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "1a2b3c4d-5e6f-4a7b-8c9d-0e1f2a3b4c5d",
    "name": "LedgerOne - Inventory (Product Category)",
    "description": "Inventory module (Product Category) API collection (Create, Get, Update, List). Reflects the implementation exactly as shipped in apps/api/src/shared/inventory.\n\nDesign note (tenant-owned, X-Tenant-Id always required): every Inventory route sits behind jwt-auth.middleware.ts AND current-tenant.middleware.ts mounted with `{ rewriteHeaderAs: \"decimal\" }` (module-registry.ts) — unlike Accounting's Currency (platform-owned, no tenant header at all), every Inventory endpoint requires both a verified Bearer token and a resolvable tenant.\n\nDesign note (X-Tenant-Id is rewritten in place, mirroring Exchange Rate exactly): because current-tenant.middleware.ts's `rewriteHeaderAs: \"decimal\"` option overwrites the `x-tenant-id` header in place with the server-verified JWT claim BEFORE this module's own `tenantIdHeaderSchema` ever inspects it, a request with a missing or malformed `X-Tenant-Id` header does NOT itself fail validation — the same documented behavior already established by Accounting's Exchange Rate/Tax Group/Tax Rule collections (see Currency.postman_collection.json's own design note). This collection therefore does not include a dedicated 'missing/malformed X-Tenant-Id' failure case for Product Category; the header is still sent on every request below purely for documentation/readability, and a genuinely missing Authorization Bearer token (checked by jwt-auth.middleware.ts, which runs BEFORE current-tenant.middleware.ts) still 401s as normal.\n\nDesign note (hierarchy-level name uniqueness, Ch.35.8): Product Category name uniqueness is scoped to the SAME Company AND the SAME parent (including two root-level Categories that both have no parent) — not Company-wide. This collection creates a Primary (root) and Second (root) Product Category, a Child Product Category nested under the Primary, and demonstrates that the Child's name is allowed to collide with a root-level name because they sit at different hierarchy levels. There is no delete endpoint for Product Category, so a collection-level pre-request script derives a `{{pcSuffix}}` from the current timestamp (once per Newman invocation) appended to every created name, avoiding cross-run collisions — a simplified version of Currency's own `Date.now()`-based uniqueness trick (no base26 ISO-code algorithm needed here, plain names suffice).\n\nDesign note (response omits parentProductCategoryUuid, a documented Handbook Deviation, not a bug): product-category.response.dto.ts deliberately omits `parentProductCategoryUuid` from the response entirely (an extra Repository lookup per row this milestone's controllers may not make) — mirrored from Account Group's/Tax Rule's/Exchange Rate's own carried-forward reasoning. This collection's success tests assert `defaultTaxGroupUuid`/`companyUuid`/`name`/timestamps are present but never assert on `parentProductCategoryUuid`'s presence or absence in the body beyond the PK-003 internal-field checks (which cover `id`/`tenantId`/`createdBy`/`updatedBy`/`deletedAt`, a different and unrelated set of fields).\n\nRun order for a full pass, top to bottom: {{productCategoryUuid}}/{{productCategoryName}} and {{secondProductCategoryUuid}}/{{secondProductCategoryName}} must both be set (by the two root-level 'Create ... Product Category - Success' requests) before the Child Product Category, Update, or List requests run.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
